title: creator_intro
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
<<if condition("encounter.cleared", "intro_workshop_raid")>>
    Creator: Scout. Over here. Give me a minute, I have to sit down.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "intro_training_active")>>
    Creator: Take your time. The low block first, then the sandbag. I'll stay here.
    -> Remind me how to move.
        Creator: Move left or right. Jump onto the block marked LOAD TEST. Hold Jump a little longer for more height.
    -> Remind me how to strike.
        Creator: Step off the block toward the sandbag. Face it and use your normal attack. Move close enough for the blade to reach.
        Creator: A swing in the air won't count. Watch for the bag to move when you connect.
    -> Let's stop the lesson.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "intro_training_active" false>>
        Creator: All right. You can ask to try again.
    -> ⟨keep practising⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "intro_torque_gauge_found") and not condition("world.flag_set", "intro_joints_checked")>>
    <<jump creator_intro__gauge>>
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "intro_questions_done")>>
    <<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_returning_to_bench")>>
        <<if condition("actor.arrived", "@talker")>>
            <<jump creator_intro__ready>>
        <<else>>
            Creator: I'll meet you at the bench. I need to put this down first.
        <<endif>>
    <<else>>
        Creator: I'll be at the bench when you're ready to finish. Come over when you've had enough practice.
        <<command "actor.walk_to" "@talker" "intro_bench_station" "keeps_to_its_tasks">>
        <<command "world.set_flag" "intro_returning_to_bench" true>>
    <<endif>>
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "intro_training_complete")>>
    Creator: How does the knee feel? No clicking? Good. Come over to the bench when you're ready for my questions.
    <<command "actor.walk_to" "@talker" "intro_bench_station" "keeps_to_its_tasks">>
    -> Ask your questions.
        <<jump creator_intro__questions>>
    -> Could we do the training run again?
        <<jump creator_intro__training>>
    -> ⟨take a look around⟩
<<else>>
    Creator: Can you hear me all right? Good.
    Creator: We can go through yesterday's training run again, if you'd like. Just your legs and a few strikes on the sandbag.
    -> Yes. Show me the basics.
        <<jump creator_intro__training>>
    -> I remember. Ask your questions.
        <<jump creator_intro__questions>>
    -> Who are you?
        Creator: I built you. This week I'm trying a new way of tuning you. I want to see what you remember after each change.
        <<jump creator_intro__offer>>
    -> Where am I?
        Creator: My workshop. It's a barn outside {$village}. The cows had it before me.
        <<jump creator_intro__offer>>
    -> ⟨look around first⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: creator_intro__offer
---
Creator: The practice run is there if you want it. No hurry.
-> Show me the basics.
    <<jump creator_intro__training>>
-> Ask your questions first.
    <<jump creator_intro__questions>>
-> What's up on the loft?
    Creator: My torque gauge. You can fetch it if you want to try a higher jump. The crate gets you up to the boards.
-> ⟨look around⟩
===

title: creator_intro__gauge
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Creator: That's the gauge. Hold it against your knee. ...Twelve. Other knee. ...Twelve. They match.
<<command "world.set_flag" "intro_joints_checked" true>>
Creator: Good. That's one thing I can stop worrying about.
<<jump creator_intro>>
===

title: creator_intro__training
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
<<command "world.set_flag" "intro_returning_to_bench" false>>
<<command "actor.walk_to" "@talker" "intro_practice_station" "keeps_to_its_tasks">>
Creator: I'll stand by the cart. Walk left to the low block marked LOAD TEST, then jump onto it.
Creator: Use your movement controls to move, and Jump to leave the ground. Hold Jump a little longer for more height. You only need one jump here.
Creator: Close this box and try it. You can come back to me for a reminder, or stop whenever you want.
<<command "world.set_flag" "intro_training_active" true>>
===

title: creator_intro__questions
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
Creator: The new tuning makes small changes often instead of big ones now and then. I want to know if you still answer like yourself afterwards.
Creator: First question. What's your name?
-> Scout.
    Creator: Same as yesterday. Good.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "scout_gave_its_name" true>>
-> I don't know.
    Creator: Yesterday you said Scout. I'll write down that you didn't remember. That's useful too.
Creator: Second. I hand you a wrench and ask for a hammer. What do you do?
-> Ask if you meant the wrench.
    Creator: That's what I hoped you'd say.
-> Fetch a hammer.
    Creator: Fine. Most people just hit it with the wrench.
-> Hit it with the wrench.
    Creator: I'm writing that down as "honest".
Creator: Last one. Is there anything you want to ask me?
-> Why did you build me?
    Creator: To see if this tuning works. And because I wanted to hear what you'd ask.
-> What's outside?
    Creator: {$village}. Fields, hills. The old gate up on the hill. They put steel on it last year.
Creator: That's enough for the notebook. Take a look around. I'll be at the bench when you're ready to finish.
<<command "world.set_flag" "intro_questions_done" true>>
<<command "world.set_flag" "intro_returning_to_bench" true>>
<<command "actor.walk_to" "@talker" "intro_bench_station" "keeps_to_its_tasks">>
===

title: creator_intro__ready
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
Creator: Anything else before I put the tools away?
-> Could we do the training run again?
    <<jump creator_intro__training>>
-> I'm ready to finish.
    Creator: Good. Let me just write the time—
    <<command "world.set_flag" "intro_raid_ready" true>>
-> ⟨not yet⟩
===

title: creator_intro__interrupted
---
<<present_speaker "npc_creator">>
Creator: Scout, stay clear of the door.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: alice_lane
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "alice_heard_bob_moved")>>
    Alice: Bob's camp is off the trail, and my line's down. Thank you.
    <<jump alice_lane__after>>
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    <<jump alice_lane__bob_told>>
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "alice_route_note_carried")>>
    Alice: Bob's in the woods past the village. Tell him to move the camp, and ask for my chain.
    <<jump alice_lane__topics>>
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "alice_met_scout")>>
    Alice: You're back. Are you all right?
    <<jump alice_lane__ask>>
<<else>>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_met_scout" true>>
    Alice: Hello? I heard shouting from the barn. Is he all right?
    -> He's dead. Goblins came in.
        Alice: Oh. I'm so sorry. I bought batteries off him. He talked the whole time.
        Alice: Goblins. Then they went up the track, past where Bob is camped.
        <<jump alice_lane__ask>>
    -> Who are you?
        Alice: Alice. I survey for the map office. My station's just there.
        Alice: Was that goblins? I saw some go up the track with a handcart.
        <<jump alice_lane__ask>>
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: alice_lane__topics
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
-> What did you see?
    Alice: Five goblins and a handcart with a crate on it. They went up the cart track toward the gate.
    Alice: The freight window isn't until tomorrow, so they'll be at the siding until then.
    Alice: One of them had a hammer as long as I am. I'd leave them alone.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_told_goblins" true>>
-> What are you measuring?
    Alice: The hills, the stream, the road to the gate. The office's map of {$village} is forty years old. Bob is doing the woods.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: alice_lane__ask
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
Alice: Bob, the other surveyor, is camped in the woods past the village. On the trail from the siding.
Alice: If those goblins walk that way, they walk straight through his camp. He doesn't know they're here.
Alice: I can't leave the instrument, I'm halfway through a traverse. Would you tell him to move the camp? And he has my chain.
-> I'll tell him.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_route_note_carried" true>>
    Alice: Thank you. Take a copy of my map. The woods are east of the village, past the inn.
-> What did you see?
    Alice: Five goblins and a handcart with a crate on it, up the cart track toward the gate. One had a hammer as long as I am. I'd leave them alone.
    <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_told_goblins" true>>
    Alice: Will you tell Bob? You don't have to.
    -> I'll tell him.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "alice_route_note_carried" true>>
        Alice: Thank you. Take a copy of my map. The woods are east of the village, past the inn.
    -> Not now.
        Alice: All right. The woods are east of the village, if you go that way.
-> Not now.
    Alice: All right. The woods are east of the village, if you go that way.
===

title: alice_lane__bob_told
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
<<command "world.set_flag" "alice_heard_bob_moved" true>>
Alice: You found Bob? And he's moving? Good. Then I'm done with that line.
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "alice_route_note_carried")>>
    Alice: Thank you for going.
<<else>>
    Alice: I didn't even ask you. Thank you.
<<endif>>
<<jump alice_lane__after>>
===

title: alice_lane__after
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_creator_notes_recovered")>>
    Alice: You got his case back from them. I wouldn't have gone.
<<elseif condition("encounter.cleared", "intro_freight_yard_fight")>>
    Alice: Someone said the goblins at the siding are gone. Was that you?
<<endif>>
-> What's on Bob's sheet? <<if condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    Alice: The woods and the old paths through them. He marks where people walk, not where the map says they should.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: bob_woods
---
<<present_speaker "npc_bob">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    Bob: Nearly packed. Go on, I'm fine. Thanks for coming out.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "alice_route_note_carried")>>
    Bob: Don't step on the chain. Who are you?
    -> Alice says move your camp off the trail. There are goblins at the siding.
        <<jump bob_woods__warned>>
    -> ⟨leave⟩
<<else>>
    Bob: Don't step on the chain. Who are you?
    -> Just walking through.
        Bob: Through the woods? Nobody walks through the woods. Except, this week, somebody does. I keep hearing them on the trail.
    -> What are you doing out here?
        Bob: Surveying. Alice has the hills and I have the trees. The trees are winning.
    -> There are goblins at the siding.
        <<jump bob_woods__warned>>
    -> ⟨leave him to it⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: bob_woods__warned
---
<<present_speaker "npc_bob">>
Bob: Goblins? Here? That's what's been on the trail.
Bob: All right. I'll move up by the hollow oak. Tell Alice I'll bring her chain tonight.
<<give_item "fieldsurvey" 1>>
<<command "world.set_flag" "bob_field_survey_received" true>>
Bob: Take my sheet. It has the paths through these woods on it, the real ones.
-> ⟨take the sheet⟩
===

title: hobford_hen
---
The hen looks at you with one eye, then the other, and goes back to the ground.
-> ⟨leave her⟩
===

title: hobford_sheep
---
The sheep lifts its black face, chews twice, and puts its head down to the grass again. Its fleece is very white and very light, and the wind moves it like the top of a cloud.
-> ⟨leave it⟩
===

title: hobford_lost_hen
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "valley_hen_found")>>
    The speckled hen is still here, scratching at the roots. She knows where she is now, and she has opinions about it.
    -> ⟨leave her⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "valley_hen_asked")>>
    A speckled hen, with one grey feather in her tail. The Plough's hen.
    -> ⟨tell her the Innkeeper is looking for her⟩
        <<command "world.set_flag" "valley_hen_found" true>>
        She looks at you as if you had said something obvious, and goes back to the roots. You will have to tell the Innkeeper where she is.
    -> ⟨leave her⟩
<<else>>
    A speckled hen. She is a long way from any farm.
    -> ⟨leave her⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: valley_miller
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_miller">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "valley_miller_met")>>
    <<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_creator_dead")>>
        Miller: Mind the sacks. And mind yourself. Whatever came for him might come back.
    <<else>>
        Miller: Mind the sacks.
    <<endif>>
    -> What do you grind?
        Miller: Oats, barley, wheat when there is wheat. And whatever the gate sends down that will go between two stones.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<else>>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "valley_miller_met" true>>
    Miller: You came down the bank path. Nobody comes down the bank path but the man from the barn on the hill.
    <<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_creator_dead")>>
        -> He's dead. Goblins came for something in his workshop.
            Miller: Dead.
            Miller: He owed me for six sacks of flour. I never once saw him bake.
            Miller: Goblins, this side of the gate. I'll bring the mule in tonight.
        -> ⟨say nothing⟩
            Miller: Well. Whatever you are, you're welcome to the porch. Not the flour.
    <<else>>
        -> I came from the barn.
            Miller: Then you're one of his. He talks to his machines more than he talks to us.
        -> ⟨say nothing⟩
            Miller: Well. Whatever you are, you're welcome to the porch. Not the flour.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
===

title: valley_innkeeper
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_innkeeper">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "valley_hen_returned")>>
    Innkeeper: She's back on her perch and laying out of spite. Come in any time.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "valley_hen_found")>>
    -> I found your hen. She's in the woods, by the trail.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "valley_hen_returned" true>>
        Innkeeper: The woods! She's never been past the well in her life.
        Innkeeper: I'll go and fetch her before the goblins do. Here, take a bowl of stew. Don't argue, I can see you're running low.
        <<give_item "HealthPotion" 1>>
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "valley_hen_asked")>>
    Innkeeper: Any sign of her? Speckled, one grey feather in her tail, a temper.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<else>>
    Innkeeper: Wipe your feet. Are you lost, or are you here about something that is?
    -> The board says to ask here about a hen.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "valley_hen_asked" true>>
        Innkeeper: Mine. Speckled, one grey feather in her tail. Gone since the morning the carts went by.
        Innkeeper: Goblins, the miller says. With a handcart, going east on the woods road. If she followed the noise, she's in the woods.
    -> What's the news?
        Innkeeper: Goblins on the woods road, the freight window tomorrow at noon, and the man from the barn on the hill hasn't been down for his supper.
        <<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_creator_dead")>>
            -> He won't be. He's dead.
                Innkeeper: Oh.
                Innkeeper: He always sat by the window and wrote in a little book. I'll keep the seat for a while.
            -> ⟨say nothing⟩
        <<endif>>
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: valley_trader
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_trader">>
Trader: Lamp oil, salt, batteries. Everything here came through the gate this week.
-> You were a smith.
    Trader: Twenty years. Then the gate opened, and every horse in the valley got sold to buy a ticket through it.
    Trader: I light the forge on Sundays, so it remembers what it's for.
-> Did the goblins come in here?
    Trader: Stood in the door and looked at the batteries for a long time. Bought nothing. The big one had a hammer I would have been proud of.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: valley_gatekeeper
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_gatekeeper">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "valley_gatekeeper_met")>>
    Gatekeeper: The freight window is tomorrow, at noon. It is always tomorrow, at noon.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<else>>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "valley_gatekeeper_met" true>>
    Gatekeeper: Name, origin, purpose.
    -> I don't have a name. I came from the barn on the hill.
        Gatekeeper: "No name, the barn, unknown." That will do. Most of them are like that.
    -> Did goblins come this way with a handcart?
        Gatekeeper: Five of them. No papers. They went down the freight track to the siding to wait for the window.
        Gatekeeper: I wrote them down as "freight". Nobody argued.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: valley_knight
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_knight">>
Knight-Errant: Stand back, it's on. It's always on. I can't find where it goes off.
-> Where did you get a laser sword?
    Knight-Errant: The gate goods shop, between the lamp oil and the salt. I traded my father's sword for it. He took it badly. So did the scabbard.
    Knight-Errant: I had the smith put a proper crossguard on it. It was only a handle. You can't swear an oath on a handle.
-> What do you use it for?
    Knight-Errant: Rats, mostly. The cellar rats of this valley have never been so frightened, or so well done.
    Knight-Errant: When it's charged I'm going up to the barrow on the moor, past the fell. Nobody has come out of it with anything. I'll be the first with a light.
-> There are goblins at the siding. <<if not condition("encounter.cleared", "intro_freight_yard_fight")>>
    Knight-Errant: I know. I'm waiting for it to charge. It charges in the Plough's window, when there's sun.
-> You could have helped with the goblins. <<if condition("encounter.cleared", "intro_freight_yard_fight")>>
    Knight-Errant: You did it with your hands? No sword at all?
    Knight-Errant: Never mind the barrow. I'm putting this back on the shelf and asking for my father's sword back.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: valley_wizard
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_wizard">>
Hedge Wizard: Don't touch the book. The book is very old. Nearly a year.
-> What book?
    Hedge Wizard: The Book of Sums. Ask it anything with a number in. Seven times eight. *he presses it* Fifty-six. Every time. Every single time.
    Hedge Wizard: Forty years I had three charms: one for warts, one for lost keys, one for a fair wind on a Tuesday. Now I have every sum there is.
-> Is it magic?
    Hedge Wizard: It came through the gate in a crate of forty, so no. Magic is rare. This is common. That's what frightens me about it.
-> Do you know any real spells?
    Hedge Wizard: Three. I've just told you all of them.
    Hedge Wizard: The Tuesday one is quite good.
-> The man in the barn. <<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_creator_dead")>>
    Hedge Wizard: He could make a thing that talks back. I can make a wart go. I'd have liked to compare notes.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: valley_ranger
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_ranger">>
Ranger: Quiet. You're standing on the trail.
-> What are you tracking?
    Ranger: Goblins. They go through batteries like bread. *she holds one up* Still warm. They went up the hill path an hour ago.
    Ranger: My grandmother tracked by bent grass. I'd like to see her try it on goblins.
-> What's that on your head?
    Ranger: A head torch. It came through the gate. It lights the way, scares the deer, and tells every goblin in the woods exactly where I am.
    Ranger: I'm still deciding if that's good.
-> The goblins at the siding are beaten. <<if condition("encounter.cleared", "intro_freight_yard_fight")>>
    Ranger: I saw the batteries stop. Thank you. Now I've nothing to follow but deer, and the deer can see me coming.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: valley_shepherd
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_shepherd">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "valley_shepherd_met")>>
    Shepherd: Forty-one. Forty-two. Don't stand there, you're putting me off.
    -> What can you see from up here?
        Shepherd: The whole valley. The mill, the Plough's chimney, the woods, the gate. Past the gate, nothing. The weather doesn't go through it either.
    -> One of your sheep is in the sky. <<if condition("world.flag_set", "hobford_sheep_clouded")>>
        Shepherd: I saw. That was forty-three.
        Shepherd: A fell sheep goes up when it goes. The fleece is too light to stay down without a sheep inside holding on.
        Shepherd: Half the weather in this valley is my grandfather's flock. I'd thank you not to add to it.
    -> Why do your sheep look like clouds? <<if not condition("world.flag_set", "hobford_sheep_clouded")>>
        <<jump valley_shepherd__clouds>>
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<else>>
    <<command "world.set_flag" "valley_shepherd_met" true>>
    Shepherd: You climbed the fell for the view? Nobody climbs the fell for the view. They climb it for a sheep.
    -> The dog in the meadow. Is it yours?
        Shepherd: She's minding the hut. She minds everything. She'd mind the gate if they let her near it.
    -> Why do your sheep look like clouds?
        <<jump valley_shepherd__clouds>>
    -> Did you see goblins come past the siding?
        Shepherd: Five, with a handcart. They sat on their crate and ate the bread I'd left on the wall.
        <<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_creator_dead")>>
            Shepherd: And you're from the barn. I heard. I'm sorry. He waved at me every morning, and I never once waved back.
        <<endif>>
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: valley_shepherd__clouds
---
<<present_speaker "npc_valley_shepherd">>
Shepherd: Because one day they will be. A fell sheep that dies goes up, fleece and all. That's what the fleece is for, as far as anyone knows.
Shepherd: The cloud on the top most mornings isn't mist. That's the old flock, keeping an eye on the young one.
Shepherd: When the gate opened, the gatekeeper wanted to stamp them as exports. I said, you catch one.
-> ⟨go⟩
===

title: hobford_dog
---
The dog sniffs your knee for a long time. Then it wags.
-> ⟨scratch its ears⟩
===

title: oiler_intro
---
<<present_speaker "npc_oiler">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "p1_stabilizer_received")>>
    Oiler: Knee holding? Good. Sit on the bench if you need to. It's mine, but I'm not using it.
    -> ⟨move on⟩
<<else>>
    Oiler: Hold still. That knee's on crooked. Who put you together?
    -> A man in {$village}. He's dead.
        <<jump oiler_intro__repair>>
    -> I'm fine.
        Oiler: You're walking like a shopping cart. Hold still.
        <<jump oiler_intro__repair>>
    -> ⟨keep walking⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: oiler_intro__repair
---
<<present_speaker "npc_oiler">>
<<portrait_clip "inspecting">>
Oiler: ...A shim and some grease. It'll hold until something hits it.
<<command "world.set_flag" "p1_stabilizer_received" true>>
Oiler: {$village}, you said? The farm gate? Huh. Long way to come with a knee like that.
-> ⟨thank him⟩
===

title: news_board_lab_incident
---
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ BREAK-IN AT A WORKSHOP NEAR {$village}. ONE DEAD. NO OTHER DAMAGE.
-> ⟨read further⟩
    <<jump news_board_lab_incident__1>>
-> ⟨walk away⟩
===

title: news_board_lab_incident__1
---
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ THE GATE AUTHORITY REMINDS CARRIERS THAT THE FARM GATES ARE FOR LICENSED FREIGHT.
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ GATE SIX: DELAYED. SOUP: TUESDAYS.
-> ⟨leave the board to its work⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple
---
Gate Janitor: Mind the wet patch. Maintenance has this corridor today, so half the signs are turned around.
-> What's that shimmer?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__1>>
-> Where do the stable gates lead?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__2>>
-> What do you actually do?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__3>>
-> Who gets priority on a busy gate?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__priority>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__1
---
Gate Janitor: Don't touch the shimmer. It won't take you anywhere. Gate Six works; use that if you need a gate.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__2
---
Gate Janitor: Six goes to a beach. Seven goes to some meeting room. Eight still says Tuesday. I stopped asking.
Gate Janitor: Seven's on the Math line now. Its breaker's on the wall; throw it and Seven dials TANGENT, and nothing else.
<<command "world.set_flag" "gate.known.TANGENT" true>>
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__3
---
Gate Janitor: Six jammed twice this morning. Seven leaks blue light. I'm here until both stop doing that.
Gate Janitor: And I mop. People walk out of a gate and lose breakfast. Robots never do. I like robots.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list
---
Manifest Clerk: Name? ...No entry. Spell it again. Slower.
-> What are the manifests for?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__1>>
-> What came through this morning?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__2>>
-> Who else has the manifest?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__copies>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__1
---
Manifest Clerk: Freight. Every crate through these gates has a line on a manifest. You're not on one. I checked twice, which is once more than I'm paid for.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__2
---
Manifest Clerk: A goblin crew filed for the {$village} freight window. One crate, one lab of research, paid in advance. Their papers were in order. Their spelling wasn't.
Manifest Clerk: Next question.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__priority
---
Gate Janitor: Medical, if the dispatcher reads the red tag. Military, when they come down and tell him to move aside.
Gate Janitor: I watched a box of spare boots go through while a man waited with medicine for his kid. I told him to file a complaint. He laughed at me.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__copies
---
Manifest Clerk: We keep one copy here and one at the {$village} gate office. I corrected the address on ours.
Manifest Clerk: {$village} sent it back marked DENIED. That's all I can show you.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
